[{'type': 'text', 'text': 'I have fixed the code in `retry.py` to handle the `Retry-After` header case-insensitively.\n\nThe original implementation was only looking for the lowercase key `"retry-after"`. I updated `parse_retry_after` to iterate through the headers and perform a case-insensitive comparison of the keys.\n\n```python\ndef parse_retry_after(headers):\n    """Seconds to wait before retrying, or None if the header is absent."""\n    for key, value in headers.items():\n        if key.lower() == "retry-after":\n            return int(value)\n    return None\n```\n\nI verified the fix by running the tests:\n```bash\npython -m pytest -q tests\n.                                                                        [100%]\n1 passed in 0.04s\n```', 'extras': {'signature': ''}}]
